# Local-only, never published: the AI collaboration logs quote internal discussion verbatim, and the
# distribution playbooks carry release detail we don't hand out. CLAUDE.md has claimed docs/ was
# ignored since the repo went public, but only commit-log/ ever was — the rest was merely untracked,
# which is one `git add .` away from being public. Ignore the folder, as documented.
docs/
# Both spellings on purpose. A trailing slash does not match a SYMLINK named docs, and a symlink is
# exactly what a git worktree needs here: the fixture tests reach docs/fixtures through #filePath, and
# a fresh worktree has no docs/ precisely because of the line above. Every agent working in one is
# told to `ln -s ../../../docs docs`, which then shows as untracked and is one `git add .` away from
# publishing a link to a local-only folder in a PUBLIC repo.
docs
# Sprint orchestration state — a working file for the run in progress, not a repo artifact.
.ww-w-ai/
# Where Scripts/gen-script-ranges.py parks the UCD files it downloads. The GENERATED table is
# committed; its 1.3 MB of input is not, because the generator re-fetches it on demand and the
# version it was built from is stamped into the output.
.ucd-cache/

# Personal test-document collection — real files, some with sensitive content. Local only.
/testdocs/
